WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.770
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.090
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.620
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.880
Hey, aren't there too many people here?

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.010
Don't sweat the small stuff!

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.080
That's right!

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.890
That's peanuts compared to Utau-chan's worries.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.190
So that means Utau-chan will be 
paying us a visit this time, right?

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.740
Yep! She's searchin' for Ikuto.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:24.970
Doki!

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.180
Yes! Yes!

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.100
Let's go!

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.110
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.900
Shugo, shugo! Yes!

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.600
Swing your arms! Hop, step, jump!

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:52.140
Now start marching straight ahead!

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.750
Way too awesome! Yes!

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.270
Every dream I've ever had!

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.980
Since they're all actually coming true.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:11.100
What kind of person will I be today?

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:16.390
What counts is being true to yourself!

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.540
Going somewhere?

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.960
Take it to the finish!

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.450
You'll always be able to

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.390
unlock your heart.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.350
So keep on changing!

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.760
It's so exciting!

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:42.890
Let's go forward, believing in our hearts!

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.620
Straight ahead!

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.280
Yeah! Yeah!

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.850
Utau?

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.140
Come to think of it, I haven't 
seen her since that concert.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.340
Hey, have you seen Utau lately?

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:18.830
Nope.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:19.680
Why not?

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.660
Don't you get it?

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.120
Ikuto's trying to protect Uta-

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.020
I have my reasons.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.350
But Utau seems to get lonely when 
she doesn't see you for a long time...

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.350
At least she's not prone to violence when 
we're together, unlike a certain someone.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:41.740
Confiscated!

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.520
But there's still some left-nya!

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.750
If Utau saw this...

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.910
We would have quite the predicament.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.890
Utau?!

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:02.890
Episode 75
The Jig is Up!? Utau Pays a Visit!

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.760
Why...

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.950
Why are you at my house?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.880
Me and Il're here, too.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.070
Yo!

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.060
I've come to talk about Ikuto.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.060
The jig's up already?!

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:21.060
Oh? Could it be that you're hiding 
Ikuto somewhere around here?

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.280
If looks could kill, I'd be dead!

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.140
No, that's simply impossible.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.970
I've really got to stop being so 
paranoid when it comes to him.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.790
Amu, are you free to head out right now?

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:38.710
You are, right?

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:42.110
U-Uh, sure, but I'd have to get ready...

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.430
Okay, go for it.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.250
But make it quick.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.710
Man, is she bossy.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.060
Any of y'all kids lost out there? Any of y'all-

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.330
Did you find one?

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.210
Stubborn Ramen?

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.850
Hinamori Amu!

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.100
That's...

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.240
That there's Ikuto's kid sister!

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.950
The loser who was kicked 
out of Easter, right?

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.280
Sure don't wanna end up like her.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.970
But you could be lookin' 
at your future self there.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.600
I'm the one using Easter!

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.310
Once I find the Embryo, <i>I'll</i> 
be saying "so long" to <i>them!</i>

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.480
Welco-

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:35.970
Salt. Noodles extra-firm. Extra back fat. Topping: seasoned egg.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.010
Comin' right up!

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.460
What did she just say?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.090
No clue.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.170
A password?

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.880
And for you, little lady?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.020
Uh, I'll have what she's having...

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.050
Hey, isn't she that idol?

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:46.810
It couldn't be.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.220
Hey, shouldn't you be in disguise?

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.130
Like a hat or some sunglasses?

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:54.970
Why should I have to sneak around when 
I haven't done anything wrong?

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:58.270
Here ya go! Two salt ramen 
with noodles extra-firm.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.860
This is good!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.950
This is my first time at an authentic ramen shop.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.820
My family only ever goes to chain 
restaurants. This feels much more grown-up!

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.880
Hit me up with more noodles, extra-firm.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.250
You ate it already?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.020
Wait, are you sure about that? 
Idols shouldn't eat so much!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.490
And why's that? I eat what I want, 
and that's all there is to it.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.890
I have to keep my strength up 
or I can't project my voice, you know.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.760
Utau's lined up the recording of her new song.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.720
She's gotta charge up her power!

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.790
Oh, you're releasing a new song!

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.270
That's what she's been slaving 
for day in and day out.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.880
We're gonna hit the big time! Once the new song comes out, we're starting a massive campaign!

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.430
We'll be very, very busy.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:49.110
So, will you be making TV appearances?

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.240
It's difficult to get on the major programs.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.600
I see...

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.690
It doesn't really matter to me where I sing,

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:59.780
because I make my stage wherever I am!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.140
Utau, you're so cool!

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.390
What's with you, freak?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:11.360
Those two are pretty chummy, huh?

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.770
Who'd a thunk it?

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.460
Feelin' a bit jealous there?

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.900
Huh? As if! No way!

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.140
One order of rice.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:23.500
Yes'm!

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.830
You're gonna eat more?!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:26.640
Blasphemy.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:35.620
In my view, someone who orders rice at 
a ramen shop is insulting the owner.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.310
Now, I don't really...

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.680
Hey, that's Maruyama-kun!

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:40.640
Who?

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:46.950
Maruyama Haruki! The charismatic elementary school gourmet who started up his own ramen blog!

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:48.840
Looks like it.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.310
So why, exactly, can't I order rice?

00:06:55.480 --> 00:07:00.820
Proper dining etiquette dictates that you should eat while the food is still hot, and never add unnecessary flavor.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.880
While you are eating the rice, the ramen will cool.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.310
And I can't recommend extra noodles, either.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.490
Please, tell me more.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:12.430
About this "proper dining etiquette" of yours.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:16.640
Certainly, though this is only my personal opinion.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:24.080
First, after the ramen is served, pause to appreciate 
the color of the broth and the gloss of the noodles.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:28.190
Then, enjoy the true flavor and 
aroma of the soup by itself!

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:32.180
Next, take a large portion of noodles...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.470
and slurp them!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:37.180
The noodles, soup, and toppings 
must be eaten in a balanced fashion.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:42.410
<i>That</i> is the proper method to eat ramen!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.350
But does it really taste best that way?

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.310
Thanks for the food.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.380
Let's go.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:56.600
Ah, wait for me!

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:13.740
I've got a hankerin' that 
there kid's a lost one!

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.350
Man, that kid was really 
something, don't you think?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.290
Well, I'll give him points 
for passion, at least.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.220
Oh yeah...

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.940
Um, didn't you say you 
wanted to talk about Ikuto?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.190
I've been searching for him a while
now, but I can't find him anywhere.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.400
And Easter's been staking out 
the area around the house.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.530
Are they trying to make 
Ikuto do something?

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:37.760
I don't know.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:42.500
Hey, why does he have to work for Easter?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.900
To compensate for what Tsukiyomi Aruto did, I presume.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.470
Tsukiyomi Aruto?

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:53.470
A long time ago, he was known as one of Japan's most preeminent violinists. He was truly gifted.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.590
He's our real father.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.730
And our mother, Hoshina Souko,

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:06.480
is the only daughter of the Hoshina family, who founded Easter.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.140
Easter?

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:12.330
Everyone around her fiercely 
opposed the idea of her

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.430
marrying a young man lacking 
status and accomplishments.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.300
But the two of them 
got married anyway,

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:24.930
on the condition that, when the time came, he would quit music and take over the family business.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.150
But he didn't honor that promise.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:36.620
He disappeared the night Grandfather, the former president of Easter, passed away.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.870
Taking only his favorite violin.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:45.830
There was great pressure 
on us, the family he'd left behind.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.340
But we waited, believing 
he'd come back to us.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:54.930
And then, a number of years ago, his violin alone was found overseas.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.560
Our mother's wearied heart 
had reached its limit.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.480
And so...

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.870
She betrayed us.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:09.630
She was remarried to Easter's director.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:20.970
My mother's always been weak, so from the 
day that man became our stepfather,

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.870
to atone for the sins 
of our father, we've been-

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.730
What? But you two had nothing to do with it!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.640
Don't you think it's weird to have to take 
responsibility for your father's actions?

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.640
You really are just a kid, aren't you?

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.580
These things happen in this world.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:43.160
Powerless children like us,
or those weak-willed like our mother...

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.430
They get crushed flat by the mighty and powerful.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:49.600
And that's why I wanted the Embryo.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.440
To save Ikuto from this cruel fate!

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:01.250
But I came to understand...

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:06.970
That I wasn't as strong as I thought.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:11.900
That I couldn't expect to save someone 
else when I couldn't even save myself.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.610
I know that now.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.090
All thanks to you.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.700
N-No way, I didn't really...

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.060
Be quiet! Just shut up 
and listen, all right?

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:25.230
But...

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.280
Seriously, be quiet!

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.450
Really?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:31.350
Hinamori-san!

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.830
Tadase-kun!

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.020
Oh, and Kukai...

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.330
We're extras now?!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.930
T-Taking a walk with Utau-chan?

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:43.220
A-Are you heading out somewhere, Tadase-kun?

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.280
S-Souma-kun and I went to a movie.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.050
Wow, this is...

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:51.760
Hey, how long have you two been so close?

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:55.360
We're not. We were just on our way back 
from getting some tonkatsu ramen.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.140
Idols eat tonkatsu ramen?

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:58.640
That a problem?

00:11:58.930 --> 00:11:59.840
Not at all!

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.810
I love ramen, too!

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:04.610
Have you heard about the new shop 
in front of the train station?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.200
If you take their super large ramen 
challenge and finish it all, it's free!

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.470
Challenge?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:12.300
Are you actually challenging me, boy?

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.470
Oh? We've got a feisty one here.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:19.430
Uh, Utau?! Are you going to eat <i>again?!</i>

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.060
There they go...

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:23.810
They seem to have hit it off.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:27.800
Since we're here and all, would 
you like to take a little walk?

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.170
S-Sure.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:36.520
Since we're here and all, we should pay extra close attention!

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.520
You got that right!

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.100
Sheesh...

00:12:54.060 --> 00:13:02.770
Tadase-kun and I both love each other... 
B-But why does everything feel so different?

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:03.730
Amu-chan.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:04.920
Y-Yes?

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:08.350
I can call you that, right?

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:13.210
S-Sure...

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:13.850
Really?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.850
Okay then... Amu-chan!

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:25.220
Amu-chan?

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.120
Yes?

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.930
Thanks for the other day.

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:35.350
I'm really glad you accepted 
my selfish confession.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:39.600
So, I was thinking about us 
starting to go out and all that...

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:47.380
I don't want to bother you or anything, and it's not 
fair to Sanjo-kun, who expressed his feelings first.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:56.440
But starting now, I want to grow to 
love you even more than I already do.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:02.850
And hopefully, you'll come to love 
me as well, if only bit by bit.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:10.580
A-All this "love" talk is kind of e-embarrassing...

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:15.660
No, I'm going to say it. I've decided to 
say it a lot to make up for the past.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.400
I love you, Amu-chan.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.020
I love <i>you</i>.

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:29.390
That's all for today, but I'm 
going to repeat it every day.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:31.070
As often as I can.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.730
Enough to make up for the 
days before I even met you.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.520
Who knew the Prince could be so aggressive!

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.530
Who knew Utau could be so aggressive!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.870
Of course she can!

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.600
And you ate tonkatsu 
ramen earlier, too. Awesome!

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:54.350
This is nothing special.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.950
That's the spirit!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.720
So the second shop gets how many stars?

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.360
Maybe the flavor was a bit too strong...

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.450
That's the girl from before!

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:12.390
She's still eating?

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:14.930
Welcome!

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:23.040
She's sure enjoying herself.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:29.680
No! That way of eating ramen is blasphemy!

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:36.630
You're lost, aren't you?

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:44.570
All you want is to believe that 
your way is the right way.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:55.380
Just do what y'all wanna do!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.560
? Character Change!

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.650
Character Transformation: Gourmet Dream!

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.680
I shall master the way of ramen!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.450
This feeling...

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.170
Utau!

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.930
Kukai, it's a ? Egg!

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:24.810
What?

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:26.810
This match is put on hold.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:27.800
Let's go.

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:28.520
Right!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.520
Stubborn Old Man Ramen Stand?

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:41.110
Don't drink water before you eat!

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:43.850
You won't be able to taste the soup!

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.080
Don't just eat the toppings first!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.970
The soup, noodles, and toppings must be eaten in proper proportion!

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:52.970
And what type of "stubborn old man" are you, forgiving such irresponsible customers?!

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:57.810
You have no right to eat or make ramen!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:04.540
That kid...

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:05.310
Do you know him?

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.990
Utau, Kukai!

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.050
That's the kid from the ramen shop.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:14.220
Amu-chan, may I handle this, please?

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.550
My heart:

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.680
My heart:

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.350
Unlock!

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:43.290
Character Transformation: Platinum Royal!

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:48.290
Character Transformation: Amulet Clover!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.020
Kukai, let's go!

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:54.250
Sorry, I'm way too full...

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.720
Maruyama-kun, that's enough!

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:02.810
Don't you dare... get in my way!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:04.680
Amu-chan!

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:20.520
Tadase-kun!

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.270
Leave it to me!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.970
Pepper?

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.930
Let's spice it up a notch!

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:36.390
Adding pepper like that is blasphemy!

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:44.560
Those are extra-firm noodles! 
You won't be able to get free so easily!

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:52.640
Character Transformation: Lunatic Charm!

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:53.870
Utau!

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:56.020
Long time no Character Transformation!

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:01.850
Nobody asked to be bound 
by your made-up rules!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:06.430
What's wrong with teaching people 
the proper way to eat ramen?!

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:18.700
There's more where that came from! 
Even more extra-firm noodles!

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.520
Noodle Wire! {Capitalized as a proper attack name~}

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:26.350
Nightmare Lorelei!

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:35.810
I've decided to do things my own way!

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:39.220
But! The proper way to eat ramen...

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:43.730
There is no "proper way" to eat something! 
Get rid of that boring old mindset!

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:46.720
It doesn't matter how you eat ramen, 
as long as you enjoy it!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:54.040
As long as you enjoy it? That's...

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:59.400
Negative Heart: Lock On!

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:05.340
Open Heart!

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.320
Now now...

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:38.550
Just gobble up some of Nagoya's special 
kishimen and you'll feel right as rain.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:41.930
Yeah, kishimen with miso and stew 
and fried shrimp, you betcha!

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.390
Wow, this is great!

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:50.960
An order of rice!

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:51.390
Comin' right up!

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:56.660
Thanks for today, Utau. You're a life-saver.

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.890
And Maruyama-kun seems 
to be feeling a lot better.

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:00.930
It's because of you.

00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:06.460
You annoy me, but you've got this strange ability.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:10.790
People like you always end up 
helping everyone around them.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.560
It's your responsibility.

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.740
So, if it's you...

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:22.810
I <i>suppose</i> I could allow 
you the right to help save Ikuto.

00:21:24.790 --> 00:21:27.810
Huh? Responsibility? Right?

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:29.820
What, you got a problem with that?

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:33.450
Of course I'd prefer to be the 
only one who protects him!

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:34.720
Don't just decide that!

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:39.290
Oh, why can't you just zip it and be grateful?!

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.860
G-Grateful for what?!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.510
Just shut up already! Jeez!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.270
We'll walk this path,

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:30.060
no matter what may happen.

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:34.350
Because when we combine our strength,

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:38.270
something's bound to change!

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:53.580
You're always so quick to say "absolutely,"

00:22:54.090 --> 00:22:57.950
but shouldn't you think it through a bit first?

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:01.330
Can't you at least do that???

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:06.080
You know, I'm starting to understand

00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:09.540
the delicate movements of the heart.

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:17.000
My own abilities aren't really all that special...

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:22.300
But even if the first shot's off the mark

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:26.170
the third'll bravely hit the bull's-eye!

00:23:28.280 --> 00:23:32.260
We'll walk this path,

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:35.880
even if it's a steep climb.

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:40.350
Because when we put our hearts together

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:44.300
something definitely changes!

00:23:50.310 --> 00:23:53.510
For some reason, 
I feel like eating ramen.

00:23:53.510 --> 00:23:56.600
But hey, is ramen a meal or a snack?

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:57.880
A meal!

00:23:57.880 --> 00:24:00.990
But sometimes it is eaten as a snack.

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:03.350
Well, as long as it tastes good, who cares?

00:24:04.450 --> 00:24:07.470
Wait, we don't have time for this!

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:09.980
There's a suspicious presence up ahead!

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:12.060
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.060 --> 00:24:14.600
A New Enemy!? Battle on a Moonlit Night!

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:16.550
Those two are in big trouble!

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:18.620
Huh? What happened?
